refurbished pacemakers: 17 years followup of an international collaborative programme</article-title><source>Stimucoeur</source><year>2003</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>190</fpage><lpage>193</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="R9"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Linde</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Bocray</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Jonsson</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Re-used pacemakers - as safe as new? A retrospective case-control study</article-title><source>Eur Heart J</source><year>1998</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>154</fpage><lpage>157</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9503189</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R10"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Havia</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Schuller</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The re-use of previously implanted pacemakers</article-title><source>Scand J Thorac Cardiovasc Surg Suppl</source><year>1978</year><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>34</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">102026</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Number of pacemakers Implanted in Selected Countries (2001)</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ipej070192-01"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Data from Mond et al [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="R1">1</xref>]</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>